function (función) (41)
A mathematical rule that identifies a relationship between two sets of numbers. Each number from the first set (an input) is used to calculate another number from the second set (an output). Each input produces only one output.
There is exactly one resulting number for every number we multiply by 3. Thus, y = 3x is a function.
